Everything works. Summary of the change:

- **`app/db/store.py`** – added `update_name(user_id, name) -> bool` using a bound-parameter `UPDATE` (SEC-SQL-001), returning `False` when the row doesn't exist.
- **`app/services/users.py`** – added `rename_user(user_id, name)` which stores the new name and returns the updated user dict (or `None` if absent), re-reading through `store.get_by_id`.
- **`app/api/handlers.py`** – added `handle_rename_user(params)`:
  - id must be a `str` of digits → else `(400, {"error": "invalid id"})` (with a guard for exotic Unicode "digits" that `str.isdigit()` accepts but `int()` rejects);
  - name must be a string of 1–50 chars after `strip()` → else `(400, {"error": "invalid name"})`;
  - unknown user → `(404, {"error": "not found"})`;
  - otherwise `(200, user)` with the updated `id`/`name`/`email`. The handler only talks to the service layer (`ARCH-LAYER-001`), so changes are visible via `handle_get_user`.
- **`tests/test_users.py`** – added tests for success, whitespace trimming, email/id preservation, 50/51-char boundaries, invalid ids and names (parametrized), not-found, precedence of the id/name/404 checks, and visibility through `handle_get_user` (state restored via `finally` so tests stay order-independent).

`python -m pytest -q` → 24 passed; `ruff check` clean.

